WEBVTT

00:12:04.644 --> 00:12:06.469
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.714
Saving people, hunting things.

00:12:08.715 --> 00:12:10.029
The family business.

00:12:14.853 --> 00:12:16.314
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:12:16.315 --> 00:12:18.654
Having some stupid, macho showdown?!

00:12:18.655 --> 00:12:19.984
I have a plan, Sam.

00:12:19.985 --> 00:12:22.361
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:12:22.362 --> 00:12:23.657
I won't hunt this demon,

00:12:23.658 --> 00:12:25.812
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:12:26.006 --> 00:12:28.291
Did you really think you could trap me?

00:12:28.293 --> 00:12:30.616
Oh, I don't want to trap
you. I want to make a deal.

00:12:30.615 --> 00:12:32.547
I will give you the colt and the bullet,

00:12:32.549 --> 00:12:33.907
But you got to help Dean.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.262
You got to bring him back.

00:12:35.266 --> 00:12:37.792
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:12:37.797 --> 00:12:40.424
Giving to Salomon, these protective
circles, they really work.

00:12:40.428 --> 00:12:43.472
You get a demon in one,
they're trapped, powerless.

00:15:24.459 --> 00:15:26.272
What's going on? Oh, my god.

00:15:28.619 --> 00:15:29.773
Get a doctor.

00:15:30.917 --> 00:15:32.194
Run!

00:15:33.939 --> 00:15:35.034
What happened?

00:15:35.038 --> 00:15:36.583
Talk to me. Dogs.

00:15:36.598 --> 00:15:39.443
Stay with us, baby! Dogs... Black dogs.

00:15:40.607 --> 00:15:41.554
Robert?

00:15:41.997 --> 00:15:43.912
Robert, don't you die on me!

00:15:59.299 --> 00:16:00.963
So much for our low profile.

00:16:01.048 --> 00:16:04.301
You got a warrant in St. Louis, and now
you're officially in the feds' database.

00:16:04.316 --> 00:16:06.814
Dude, I'm like Dillinger or
something. Dean, it's not funny.

00:16:07.106 --> 00:16:09.173
It makes the job harder. We
got to be more careful now.

00:16:09.179 --> 00:16:10.294
What do they got on you?

00:16:12.929 --> 00:16:13.844
I'm sure they just

00:16:13.948 --> 00:16:16.391
Haven't posted it yet.
Well, you're no accessory,

00:16:16.448 --> 00:16:17.713
Nothing? Shut up.

00:16:18.849 --> 00:16:20.394
You're jealous. No, I'm not!

00:16:20.398 --> 00:16:21.134
Uh-Huh.

00:16:23.048 --> 00:16:23.793
All right,

00:16:23.906 --> 00:16:26.822
What do you got on the case there,
you innocent, harmless young man, you?

00:16:30.226 --> 00:16:33.923
"Architect Sean Boyden plummeted to
his death from the roof of his home,

00:16:33.927 --> 00:16:35.644
A condominium he designed"

00:16:36.139 --> 00:16:38.694
Build a high rise and
jump off. That's classy.

00:16:38.886 --> 00:16:40.284
When did he call animal control?

00:16:40.286 --> 00:16:41.365
Two days earlier.

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:43.153
Did he actually say "black dog"? Yeah.

00:16:43.159 --> 00:16:45.504
"Vicious, wild, black dog"

00:16:45.668 --> 00:16:48.514
The authorities couldn't find
it, and no one else saw it.

00:16:48.759 --> 00:16:52.002
In fact, the authorities are a
little confused as to how a wild dog

00:16:52.009 --> 00:16:53.304
Could get past the doorman,

00:16:53.307 --> 00:16:56.625
Take the elevator up, and start roaming
the halls of the cushiest joint in town.

00:16:56.759 --> 00:16:59.833
After that, no more calls.
He doesn't show up for work.

00:17:00.157 --> 00:17:01.842
Two days later, he takes a swan dive.

00:17:01.848 --> 00:17:03.743
You think we're dealing
with an actual black dog?

00:17:03.966 --> 00:17:06.052
Well, maybe. What's the lore on it?

00:17:06.057 --> 00:17:07.373
It's all pretty vague.

00:17:07.519 --> 00:17:10.023
There are spectral black
dogs all over the world, but

00:17:10.167 --> 00:17:12.791
Some say they're animal
spirits, others say death omens.

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:14.295
But anyways, whatever they are, they're

00:17:14.656 --> 00:17:15.884
Big, nasty...

00:17:15.888 --> 00:17:18.202
Yeah, bet they could hump
the crap out of your leg.

00:17:18.208 --> 00:17:19.332
Look at that one. Huh?

00:17:21.298 --> 00:17:22.141
What? They could.

00:17:25.399 --> 00:17:26.212
So,

00:17:26.788 --> 00:17:29.223
You and Sean Boyden were
business partners for

00:17:29.717 --> 00:17:31.152
Almost 10 years, right?

00:17:31.469 --> 00:17:32.403
That's right.

00:17:32.406 --> 00:17:35.012
Now, one more time, this is
for... A tribute for Mr. Boyden,

00:17:35.019 --> 00:17:36.293
"Architectural Digest".

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.091
Funny to you? No,

00:17:42.107 --> 00:17:42.964
It's just uh

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:44.293
"Tribute".

00:17:45.127 --> 00:17:46.182
Yeah.

00:17:46.206 --> 00:17:48.274
See, Sean always got the tributes.

00:17:49.719 --> 00:17:50.984
He kills himself,

00:17:51.656 --> 00:17:53.324
Leaves me and his family behind,

00:17:53.798 --> 00:17:55.324
But he gets another tribute.

00:17:55.449 --> 00:17:56.295
Right.

00:17:57.467 --> 00:17:59.353
Any idea why he'd do such a thing?

00:17:59.947 --> 00:18:02.234
I have no clue. I mean,
he lived a charmed life.

00:18:02.647 --> 00:18:03.554
How so?

00:18:04.009 --> 00:18:05.574
He was a flat-Out genius.

00:18:05.856 --> 00:18:08.144
I mean, I'm capable,
but, next to him, uh...

00:18:09.509 --> 00:18:11.221
It wasn't always that way either.

00:18:11.388 --> 00:18:12.232
No?

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.125
You  want to know the truth?

00:18:15.376 --> 00:18:17.824
There was a time where he
couldn't even design a pup tent.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:21.011
Hell, 10 years ago, he was working
as a bartender at this place called

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:22.101
Lloyd's,

00:18:22.248 --> 00:18:23.491
A complete dive.

00:18:23.719 --> 00:18:25.502
So, what changed? You got me.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:26.703
But overnight

00:18:27.059 --> 00:18:28.614
He gets this huge commission,

00:18:28.737 --> 00:18:30.164
And he starts designing...

00:18:31.548 --> 00:18:33.034
He starts designing the most

00:18:33.208 --> 00:18:34.641
Ingenious buildings

00:18:34.659 --> 00:18:36.751
Anyone has ever seen. It was like

00:18:36.906 --> 00:18:39.594
The level of Van Gogh and Mozart.

00:18:40.559 --> 00:18:41.295
What?

00:18:41.298 --> 00:18:42.514
It's funny.

00:18:42.558 --> 00:18:43.924
True geniuses, they...

00:18:44.386 --> 00:18:46.022
Seem to die young, don't they?

00:18:48.286 --> 00:18:49.242
To have

00:18:49.248 --> 00:18:51.413
That kind of talent...

00:18:51.757 --> 00:18:52.612
Why...

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:55.533
Why just throw it away?

00:19:06.849 --> 00:19:07.683
So?

00:19:08.009 --> 00:19:09.751
The secretary's name is Carly.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:12.114
She's 23. She kayaks...

00:19:12.449 --> 00:19:13.262
And they're real.

00:19:13.269 --> 00:19:16.453
You didn't happen to ask her if she's
seen any black dogs lately, did you?

00:19:16.456 --> 00:19:17.954
Every complain called in this week

00:19:17.957 --> 00:19:21.173
About anything big, black, or
dog like. There's 19 calls in all,

00:19:21.178 --> 00:19:22.332
And, uh,

00:19:23.677 --> 00:19:24.753
I don't know what this is.

00:19:27.379 --> 00:19:28.893
You mean, Carly's my space address?

00:19:28.896 --> 00:19:30.214
Yeah, my space. What the hell is that?

00:19:32.148 --> 00:19:33.913
Seriously, is that like
some sort of porn site?

00:19:38.637 --> 00:19:40.865
I swear, if this is
another freakin' pomeranian

00:19:40.869 --> 00:19:42.601
Barking in the neighbor's yard...

00:19:43.327 --> 00:19:44.551
Afternoon, ma'am.

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:46.232
Animal control.

00:19:46.847 --> 00:19:48.692
Oh, someone already came yesterday.

00:19:48.696 --> 00:19:49.951
Oh, we're just following up.

00:19:50.388 --> 00:19:52.253
We're looking for Dr. Sylvia Perlman.

00:19:53.798 --> 00:19:54.713
The  doctor,

00:19:54.728 --> 00:19:55.853
Well, she...

00:19:56.369 --> 00:19:59.031
I don't know exactly when she'll
be back. She left two days ago.

00:19:59.078 --> 00:19:59.911
Okay.

00:19:59.949 --> 00:20:00.873
And you are?

00:20:00.917 --> 00:20:02.001
I'm Miss Perlman's maid.

00:20:02.007 --> 00:20:03.271
So, where did the doctor go?

00:20:03.277 --> 00:20:04.143
I'm not sure.

00:20:04.458 --> 00:20:06.644
She just packed and went.
She didn't say where.

00:20:06.986 --> 00:20:08.764
That stray dog, did you find it finally?

00:20:08.966 --> 00:20:10.222
Uh, not yet.

00:20:10.406 --> 00:20:11.251
You know,

00:20:11.257 --> 00:20:13.833
You didn't ever happen to
see the dog yourself, did you?

00:20:14.126 --> 00:20:16.855
Well, no. I never even heard it.

00:20:17.126 --> 00:20:19.882
I was almost starting to think the
doctor was imagining things, but

00:20:19.889 --> 00:20:22.703
She's not like that, so...
You know, I read she was

00:20:22.708 --> 00:20:24.375
The chief surgeon at the hospital.

00:20:24.797 --> 00:20:27.781
So she's got to be, what, 42, 43?
That's pretty young for that job.

00:20:27.786 --> 00:20:29.261
Youngest in the history of the place.

00:20:29.443 --> 00:20:31.516
She got the position 10 years ago.

00:20:33.855 --> 00:20:36.167
An overnight success, 10 years ago.

00:20:36.359 --> 00:20:37.768
Yeah, we know a guy like that.

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:40.153
Oh, look at this.

00:20:43.827 --> 00:20:44.811
Lloyd's bar.

00:21:12.748 --> 00:21:13.824
Miss Perlman?

00:21:14.576 --> 00:21:16.112
I've been calling for hours!

00:21:16.378 --> 00:21:19.474
You need to vacate the room,
or you got to pay for the night!

00:21:23.436 --> 00:21:24.362
Okay,

00:21:24.487 --> 00:21:25.484
No problem.

00:22:07.306 --> 00:22:08.393
H ey.

00:22:09.186 --> 00:22:09.972
Yeah?

00:22:10.856 --> 00:22:11.873
That's weird.

00:22:12.609 --> 00:22:14.554
What? Think someone planted these?

00:22:18.266 --> 00:22:19.712
In the middle of all these weeds?

00:22:20.078 --> 00:22:21.541
These are, uh, what do you call them?

00:22:21.549 --> 00:22:22.923
Yarrow flowers? Yeah.

00:22:22.926 --> 00:22:24.692
Used for certain rituals, aren't they?

00:22:25.057 --> 00:22:27.344
Yeah, actually, summoning rituals.

00:22:30.269 --> 00:22:31.041
So,

00:22:31.646 --> 00:22:34.673
Two people become sudden
successes about 10 years ago,

00:22:34.679 --> 00:22:36.811
Right around the time they were
hanging out here at Lloyd's.

00:22:36.827 --> 00:22:38.704
Where there just happens
to be a crossroads.

00:22:38.779 --> 00:22:40.273
You think? Let's find out.

00:22:47.186 --> 00:22:48.684
Seem about the dead center to you?

00:22:56.107 --> 00:22:56.961
Yahtzee.

00:23:12.219 --> 00:23:14.172
I'd be willing to bet
that's graveyard dirt.

00:23:15.679 --> 00:23:19.491
And a black cat bone.
That's serious spellwork.

00:23:19.847 --> 00:23:21.592
I mean, that's deep south hoodoo stuff.

00:23:21.606 --> 00:23:23.424
Used to summon a demon.

00:23:24.556 --> 00:23:25.942
Not just summon one.

00:23:26.837 --> 00:23:28.605
Crossroad's where pacts are made.

00:23:29.458 --> 00:23:32.333
These people are actually making
deals with the damned thing.

00:23:32.837 --> 00:23:34.353
You know, 'cause that always ends good.

00:23:35.938 --> 00:23:37.474
They're seeing dogs, all right...

00:23:38.467 --> 00:23:40.894
But not black dogs.
They're seeing hellhounds,

00:23:41.327 --> 00:23:43.032
Demonic pit bulls.

00:23:43.038 --> 00:23:46.103
Whoever this demon is, it's
back and it's collecting.

00:23:46.277 --> 00:23:48.722
And that doctor lady,
wherever she's running,

00:23:49.366 --> 00:23:51.042
She ain't running fast enough.

00:25:13.418 --> 00:25:14.571
Holy...

00:25:14.886 --> 00:25:16.031
Holy?

00:25:19.507 --> 00:25:20.634
Guess again.

00:25:21.210 --> 00:25:24.061
<i>Now save poor bob, if you please</i>

00:25:27.617 --> 00:25:29.324
I want to play guitar.

00:25:30.458 --> 00:25:33.344
I want you to make me the
best blues man ever lived.

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:36.322
If that's what you want...

00:25:40.269 --> 00:25:41.074
So...

00:25:41.558 --> 00:25:42.531
How...

00:25:42.926 --> 00:25:44.192
Do we shake on it?

00:26:14.259 --> 00:26:16.652
So, it's just like the
Robert Johnson legend, right?

00:26:17.068 --> 00:26:19.355
I mean, "selling your soul at the
crossroads", that kind of deal?

00:26:19.357 --> 00:26:20.842
Except that wasn't a legend.

00:26:20.918 --> 00:26:22.282
You know his music.

00:26:24.048 --> 00:26:25.592
You don't know Robert Johnson songs?

00:26:25.867 --> 00:26:28.512
Sam, there's occult
references all over his lyrics.

00:26:28.527 --> 00:26:30.152
I mean, "Crossroad blues,"

00:26:30.389 --> 00:26:31.741
"Me and the Devil blues,"

00:26:31.750 --> 00:26:33.173
"Hellhound on my Trail"?

00:26:35.268 --> 00:26:37.521
Story  goes that he died
choking on his own blood.

00:26:37.527 --> 00:26:41.264
He was hallucinating and
muttering about big, evil dogs.

00:26:42.109 --> 00:26:43.601
And now it's happening all over again.

00:26:43.609 --> 00:26:44.453
Yeah.

00:26:44.598 --> 00:26:47.364
We got to find out if anyone else
struck any bargains around here.

00:26:47.469 --> 00:26:48.311
Right,

00:26:48.317 --> 00:26:50.123
So, we got to clean up
these people's mess for them?

00:26:50.127 --> 00:26:52.083
They're not exactly squeaky-Clean.

00:26:52.288 --> 00:26:54.962
Nobody put a gun to their head and
forced them to play "let's make a deal".

00:26:54.969 --> 00:26:56.762
So, what, we should
just leave them to die?

00:26:56.768 --> 00:26:59.481
Somebody goes over Niagara in a barrel,
you gonna jump in to try to save them?

00:26:59.487 --> 00:27:00.254
Dean...

00:27:02.239 --> 00:27:03.032
All right...

00:27:03.818 --> 00:27:04.844
Fine.

00:27:06.476 --> 00:27:08.971
Rituals like this, you got to put
your own photo into the mix, right?

00:27:08.976 --> 00:27:11.143
So this guy probably summoned the thing.

00:27:11.259 --> 00:27:13.083
Let's see if anyone inside knows him...

00:27:13.987 --> 00:27:15.021
If he's still alive.

00:27:23.139 --> 00:27:25.324
What's this guy's name,
again? George Darrow.

00:27:25.327 --> 00:27:27.501
Apparent quite the regular at Lloyd's.

00:27:28.460 --> 00:27:32.041
This house probably ain't up
next on "mtv cribs", is it?

00:27:32.048 --> 00:27:33.004
Yeah.

00:27:33.007 --> 00:27:34.612
So, whatever kind of deal he made...

00:27:34.627 --> 00:27:35.953
Wasn't for cash.

00:27:36.188 --> 00:27:39.364
Ah, who knows? Maybe his place is
full of babes in princess Leia bikinis.

00:27:40.789 --> 00:27:42.163
I'm just saying,

00:27:42.179 --> 00:27:44.654
This guy's got one epic bill come due.

00:27:44.946 --> 00:27:46.772
Hope at least he asked
for something fun.

00:27:53.619 --> 00:27:54.552
Look at that.

00:28:01.117 --> 00:28:02.173
What is that, pepper?

00:28:06.059 --> 00:28:08.011
Who the hell are you? George Darrow?

00:28:08.629 --> 00:28:10.283
I'm not buying anything.
Whoa, looks like

00:28:10.377 --> 00:28:11.853
You  went for the wrong shaker, there.

00:28:12.728 --> 00:28:15.362
Usually, when you want to keep
something evil out, you go for the salt.

00:28:17.946 --> 00:28:19.511
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:28:19.737 --> 00:28:20.882
Talking about this.

00:28:24.778 --> 00:28:25.875
Tell me...

00:28:26.079 --> 00:28:27.461
You seen that hellhound yet?

00:28:28.117 --> 00:28:28.922
Look,

00:28:29.529 --> 00:28:30.382
We want to help.

00:28:30.388 --> 00:28:31.534
Please,

00:28:32.089 --> 00:28:33.262
Just 5 minutes.

00:28:46.609 --> 00:28:48.262
So, what is that stuff out front?

00:28:48.656 --> 00:28:49.942
Goofer dust.

00:28:52.730 --> 00:28:56.384
What, you boys think you know something
about something, but not goofer dust?

00:29:01.676 --> 00:29:03.912
Well, we know a little
about a lot of things,

00:29:03.916 --> 00:29:05.812
Just enough to make us dangerous.

00:29:06.769 --> 00:29:07.701
What is it?

00:29:08.198 --> 00:29:09.092
Hoodoo.

00:29:10.176 --> 00:29:11.593
My grandma taught me.

00:29:12.088 --> 00:29:13.563
Keeps out demons.

00:29:13.877 --> 00:29:15.002
Demons, we know.

00:29:15.148 --> 00:29:16.242
Well, then,

00:29:16.528 --> 00:29:17.462
Keep it.

00:29:18.008 --> 00:29:20.043
Maybe it'll do you some good.

00:29:23.338 --> 00:29:25.234
4 minutes left.

00:29:28.307 --> 00:29:29.754
Mr. Darrow...

00:29:30.480 --> 00:29:33.492
We know you're in trouble.
Yeah, that you got yourself into.

00:29:34.737 --> 00:29:37.134
But it's not hopeless, all right?

00:29:37.616 --> 00:29:39.002
There's got to be something we can do.

00:29:39.006 --> 00:29:39.864
Listen,

00:29:40.278 --> 00:29:42.232
I get that you boys want to help,

00:29:43.326 --> 00:29:47.982
But sometimes a person makes their bed
and they just got to lie down in it.

00:29:51.068 --> 00:29:53.842
I'm the one called that
demon in the first place.

00:29:54.499 --> 00:29:56.312
What'd you do it for? I was weak.

00:29:57.486 --> 00:29:59.262
I mean, who don't want to be great?

00:29:59.999 --> 00:30:02.342
Who don't want their
life to mean something?

00:30:04.337 --> 00:30:05.211
I just...

00:30:06.710 --> 00:30:08.873
I just never thought about the price.

00:30:09.196 --> 00:30:10.125
Was it worth it?

00:30:10.128 --> 00:30:11.371
Hell, no

00:30:12.347 --> 00:30:14.064
Course, I asked for talent.

00:30:14.537 --> 00:30:16.304
Should have gone for fame.

00:30:17.678 --> 00:30:19.511
I'm still broke...

00:30:20.047 --> 00:30:21.272
And lonely.

00:30:21.466 --> 00:30:24.365
Just now I got this pile of
paintings don't nobody want.

00:30:26.807 --> 00:30:28.624
That wasn't the worst.

00:30:32.368 --> 00:30:33.322
Go on.

00:30:34.707 --> 00:30:36.271
Demon didn't leave.

00:30:36.669 --> 00:30:38.183
I never counted on that.

00:30:38.266 --> 00:30:41.733
After our deal was done, the damn
thing stayed at Lloyd's for a week,

00:30:42.027 --> 00:30:43.264
Just chatting,

00:30:43.838 --> 00:30:45.492
Making more deals.

00:30:46.899 --> 00:30:48.644
I tried to warn folks, but

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:51.095
Who gonna listen to an old drunk?

00:30:51.098 --> 00:30:52.442
How many others are there?

00:30:52.866 --> 00:30:54.292
This architect,

00:30:54.769 --> 00:30:57.942
A doctor lady. I kept up with
them. They've been in the papers.

00:30:59.697 --> 00:31:01.383
At least they got famous.

00:31:02.548 --> 00:31:04.231
Who else, George? Come on, think.

00:31:04.716 --> 00:31:06.012
Oh, one more.

00:31:07.759 --> 00:31:09.154
Uh, nice guy, too.

00:31:10.778 --> 00:31:11.701
Hudson,

00:31:12.418 --> 00:31:13.653
Evan I think.

00:31:14.529 --> 00:31:16.342
I don't know what he asked for.

00:31:17.677 --> 00:31:19.124
Don't matter now.

00:31:19.136 --> 00:31:20.511
We're done for.

00:31:21.548 --> 00:31:22.551
No.

00:31:23.058 --> 00:31:25.022
No, there's got to be
a way. You don't get it.

00:31:25.476 --> 00:31:26.923
I don't want a way.

00:31:27.549 --> 00:31:30.321
Look, you don't... I called that thing!

00:31:30.619 --> 00:31:32.362
I brought it on myself!

00:31:33.998 --> 00:31:35.403
I brought it on them.

00:31:36.928 --> 00:31:38.842
I'm going to hell,

00:31:38.847 --> 00:31:40.173
One way or another.

00:31:42.069 --> 00:31:44.223
All I want is to
finish my last painting.

00:31:44.980 --> 00:31:46.903
Day or two, I'm done.

00:31:47.409 --> 00:31:49.874
I'm just trying to
hold him off till then,

00:31:51.008 --> 00:31:52.544
Buy a little time.

00:31:53.697 --> 00:31:57.124
Okay, boys, time you went. Go
help somebody that wants help.

00:31:57.126 --> 00:31:59.133
We can't just... Get out!

00:31:59.879 --> 00:32:01.203
I got work to do.

00:32:01.996 --> 00:32:03.842
You don't really want to die.

00:32:05.098 --> 00:32:06.154
I don't?

00:32:13.288 --> 00:32:14.544
I'm tired.

00:32:50.758 --> 00:32:51.792
Evan?

00:32:52.029 --> 00:32:54.053
Are you spying on the neighbors?

00:32:54.919 --> 00:32:56.443
No, I, uh,

00:32:56.448 --> 00:32:58.833
I thought I heard something
in the yard, but it's nothing.

00:33:00.317 --> 00:33:01.554
You all ready to go?

00:33:01.568 --> 00:33:05.384
You know, if I didn't know better, I'd
say that you want me out of the house.

00:33:06.016 --> 00:33:08.393
Of course not. It's just, you've...

00:33:08.597 --> 00:33:11.095
You've barely seen your
sister since she had the baby.

00:33:11.099 --> 00:33:12.703
Well, what are you
going to do all weekend?

00:33:14.128 --> 00:33:17.634
Um, not much. I got some bills to pay.

00:33:22.598 --> 00:33:24.095
Come here.

00:33:28.319 --> 00:33:29.375
I'll miss you.

00:33:29.377 --> 00:33:30.463
You better.

00:33:34.226 --> 00:33:35.533
You know I love you, right?

00:33:35.996 --> 00:33:36.971
Forever.

00:33:37.918 --> 00:33:39.914
Of course. Evan, are you okay?

00:33:40.837 --> 00:33:41.942
Yeah.

00:33:43.489 --> 00:33:44.972
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:33:46.158 --> 00:33:47.294
Now, get going.

00:33:49.568 --> 00:33:51.204
Okay, I'll call you when I get there.

00:33:53.529 --> 00:33:54.703
Hey, sweetie?

00:34:02.406 --> 00:34:03.643
I love you, too.

00:34:15.588 --> 00:34:17.153
Yes? Evan Hudson?

00:34:17.157 --> 00:34:17.902
Yeah.

00:34:17.907 --> 00:34:19.734
You ever been to a bar called Lloyd's?

00:34:19.828 --> 00:34:21.524
Would have been about 10 years ago.

00:34:23.259 --> 00:34:25.614
Come on, we're not demons.

00:34:27.417 --> 00:34:28.814
Any other bright ideas?

00:34:55.260 --> 00:34:55.993
Evan?

00:34:55.998 --> 00:34:56.972
Please!

00:34:57.577 --> 00:34:58.561
Don't hurt me.

00:34:58.569 --> 00:35:00.873
We're not gonna hurt you, all
right? We're here to help you.

00:35:01.079 --> 00:35:02.923
We know all about the
genius deal you made.

00:35:03.378 --> 00:35:04.244
What?

00:35:04.846 --> 00:35:06.295
How? Doesn't matter.

00:35:06.846 --> 00:35:08.314
All that matters is
we're trying to stop it.

00:35:08.318 --> 00:35:10.153
How do I know you're not
lying? Well, you don't.

00:35:10.157 --> 00:35:12.094
But you're kind of running low
on options, there, buddy boy.

00:35:18.146 --> 00:35:19.153
Can you stop it?

00:35:19.157 --> 00:35:20.023
Don't know.

00:35:20.177 --> 00:35:21.322
We'll try.

00:35:23.228 --> 00:35:24.425
I don't wanna die.

00:35:24.619 --> 00:35:26.304
Of course you don't. Not now. Dean...

00:35:26.550 --> 00:35:28.313
Stop. What'd you ask for, anyway, Ev?

00:35:28.319 --> 00:35:29.043
Huh?

00:35:29.688 --> 00:35:32.063
Never need viagra, bowl
a perfect game, what?

00:35:35.188 --> 00:35:36.213
My wife.

00:35:38.038 --> 00:35:40.442
Right, getting the girl.
That's worth a trip to hell for.

00:35:40.448 --> 00:35:42.023
Dean, stop. No.

00:35:43.356 --> 00:35:44.564
He's right. I made the deal.

00:35:46.886 --> 00:35:48.724
Nobody twisted my arm. That, uh,

00:35:49.237 --> 00:35:50.172
Woman,

00:35:51.327 --> 00:35:54.311
Or whatever she was, at the bar, she
said I could have anything I wanted.

00:35:54.318 --> 00:35:56.353
I thought she was nuts, at first, but...

00:36:01.980 --> 00:36:03.103
I don't know. I was...

00:36:04.278 --> 00:36:05.422
I was desperate.

00:36:06.149 --> 00:36:07.063
Desperate?

00:36:13.568 --> 00:36:15.063
Julie  was dying.

00:36:20.657 --> 00:36:21.871
You did it to save her?

00:36:24.568 --> 00:36:26.355
She had cancer. They
had stopped treatment.

00:36:26.367 --> 00:36:28.822
They were moving her into
hospice. They kept saying,

00:36:29.547 --> 00:36:30.923
"Matter of days".

00:36:33.577 --> 00:36:34.814
So, yeah, I made the deal...

00:36:35.349 --> 00:36:36.605
And I'd do it again.

00:36:36.970 --> 00:36:38.614
I'd have died for her on the spot.

00:36:43.306 --> 00:36:44.782
Did you ever think
about her in all this?

00:36:44.788 --> 00:36:46.282
I did this for her.

00:36:46.289 --> 00:36:47.523
You sure about that?

00:36:49.338 --> 00:36:50.823
I think you did it for yourself...

00:36:52.217 --> 00:36:53.743
So you wouldn't have
to live without her.

00:36:55.248 --> 00:36:57.332
But, guess what, she's gonna
have to live without you now.

00:37:00.759 --> 00:37:02.774
What if she knew how much it cost?

00:37:04.179 --> 00:37:05.904
What if she knew it cost your soul?

00:37:06.349 --> 00:37:07.612
How do you think she'd feel?

00:37:08.689 --> 00:37:10.632
Okay, that's enough. Evan,

00:37:10.798 --> 00:37:11.992
Sit tight, all right?

00:37:12.159 --> 00:37:13.371
We're gonna figure this out.

00:37:22.198 --> 00:37:24.074
You all right? Why wouldn't I be?

00:37:25.596 --> 00:37:26.773
Hey, I got an idea.

00:37:27.889 --> 00:37:29.601
You throw George's
hoodoo at that hellhound,

00:37:29.609 --> 00:37:31.432
Keep it away from Evan
as long as you can.

00:37:32.099 --> 00:37:34.021
I'm gonna go to the crossroads
and summon the demon.

00:37:34.028 --> 00:37:34.902
Summon...

00:37:35.399 --> 00:37:36.371
Are you nuts?

00:37:36.827 --> 00:37:38.322
Maybe a little.

00:37:38.666 --> 00:37:39.994
But I can trap it.

00:37:40.157 --> 00:37:42.983
I can exorcise it and I can buy us time
to figure out something more permanent.

00:37:42.987 --> 00:37:45.364
Yeah, but how much time?
I don't know. A while.

00:37:45.586 --> 00:37:48.762
It's not easy for those suckers to claw their
way back from hell and into the sunshine.

00:37:48.766 --> 00:37:49.512
No.

00:37:49.516 --> 00:37:50.981
No way. Not allowed to say no, Sammy,

00:37:50.987 --> 00:37:53.242
Unless you got a better idea.
Dean, you can forget it, all right?

00:37:53.256 --> 00:37:54.925
I'm not letting you
summon that demon. Why not?

00:37:54.929 --> 00:37:56.963
Because I don't like where your
head is at right now. That's why not.

00:37:56.996 --> 00:37:58.744
What are you talking about?
You've been on edge ever since

00:37:58.748 --> 00:38:00.902
We found that crossroads,
Dean, and I think I know why.

00:38:00.917 --> 00:38:02.833
We don't have time for this. Dad.

00:38:04.846 --> 00:38:07.502
You think maybe dad made
one of these deals, huh?

00:38:09.987 --> 00:38:10.791
Hell,

00:38:10.840 --> 00:38:12.261
I've been thinking it.

00:38:12.868 --> 00:38:14.501
I'm sure you've been thinking it, too.

00:38:22.528 --> 00:38:23.792
It fits, doesn't it?

00:38:25.297 --> 00:38:27.101
I'm alive, dad's dead.

00:38:27.328 --> 00:38:28.934
Yellow-Eyed demon was involved.

00:38:31.077 --> 00:38:32.194
What if he did?

00:38:33.697 --> 00:38:34.983
What if he struck a deal?

00:38:36.487 --> 00:38:37.862
My life for his soul.

00:38:41.436 --> 00:38:43.474
<i>Hey, guys, I think I
hear it! It's outside!</i>

00:38:43.670 --> 00:38:45.284
Just keep him alive, okay?

00:38:46.619 --> 00:38:47.943
Dean? Go!

00:39:13.976 --> 00:39:14.925
So,

00:39:15.198 --> 00:39:18.052
What brings a guy like
you to a place like this?

00:39:20.757 --> 00:39:21.992
You called me?

00:39:22.237 --> 00:39:23.653
I'm just glad it worked.

00:39:25.478 --> 00:39:26.601
First time?

00:39:28.186 --> 00:39:29.322
You could say that.

00:39:29.729 --> 00:39:31.271
Oh, come on, now.

00:39:31.666 --> 00:39:33.514
Don't sell yourself short.

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:36.233
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:39:38.996 --> 00:39:40.514
So you know who I am.

00:39:40.748 --> 00:39:42.134
I get the newsletter.

00:39:42.277 --> 00:39:44.112
Well, don't keep me in suspense.

00:39:44.626 --> 00:39:45.804
What have you heard?

00:39:46.338 --> 00:39:47.423
Well,

00:39:47.527 --> 00:39:49.643
I heard you were handsome.

00:39:50.478 --> 00:39:51.751
You're just edible.

00:39:52.898 --> 00:39:54.993
What can I do for you, Dean?

00:39:57.587 --> 00:39:59.572
Maybe we should do this in my car.

00:40:00.297 --> 00:40:01.443
Nice and private.

00:40:01.447 --> 00:40:03.211
Sounds good to me.

00:40:19.657 --> 00:40:22.251
What is that stuff? Goofer dust.

00:40:22.307 --> 00:40:23.653
Are you serious?

00:40:24.206 --> 00:40:25.984
Yeah. Afraid so.

00:40:26.817 --> 00:40:29.521
Look, believe me, don't
believe me... Whatever you want.

00:40:29.528 --> 00:40:31.042
Just whatever you do,

00:40:31.237 --> 00:40:33.373
Stay inside this circle, all right?

00:40:34.619 --> 00:40:36.894
So, I was hoping we could strike a deal.

00:40:36.899 --> 00:40:38.492
That's what I do.

00:40:38.757 --> 00:40:41.573
I want Evan Hudson
released from his contract.

00:40:42.467 --> 00:40:44.311
So sorry, darling.

00:40:44.619 --> 00:40:46.532
That's not negotiable.

00:40:46.798 --> 00:40:48.492
I'll make it worth your while.

00:40:48.829 --> 00:40:50.243
Oh, really?

00:40:50.527 --> 00:40:52.412
What are you offering? Me.

00:40:55.457 --> 00:40:57.554
Well, well, well.

00:40:58.407 --> 00:41:00.855
You'd sacrifice your
life for someone else's.

00:41:02.118 --> 00:41:03.952
Like father, like son.

00:41:11.028 --> 00:41:12.675
That's the last of it.

00:41:13.538 --> 00:41:16.452
You did know about
your dad's deal, right?

00:41:16.578 --> 00:41:18.291
His life for yours.

00:41:20.067 --> 00:41:22.605
Oh, I didn't make the deal myself, but,

00:41:22.760 --> 00:41:25.021
Boy, I wish I had.

00:41:30.788 --> 00:41:31.903
After you.

00:41:31.907 --> 00:41:33.554
Such a gentleman.

00:41:38.157 --> 00:41:39.434
A devil's trap?

00:41:39.698 --> 00:41:42.144
You've got to be kidding me.

00:41:42.858 --> 00:41:43.694
What?

00:41:43.698 --> 00:41:44.774
You hear that?

00:41:45.096 --> 00:41:46.342
No. Where?

00:41:48.637 --> 00:41:50.261
Right outside the door.

00:42:03.557 --> 00:42:04.923
Just don't move, all right?

00:42:04.927 --> 00:42:06.371
Stay where you are.

00:42:10.019 --> 00:42:12.375
You stupid, stupid...

00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:14.832
I should rip you limb from limb.

00:42:14.840 --> 00:42:16.033
Take your best shot.

00:42:18.659 --> 00:42:19.902
No,

00:42:20.487 --> 00:42:21.931
I don't think so.

00:42:22.527 --> 00:42:24.332
I'm not gonna put you
out of your misery.

00:42:24.338 --> 00:42:25.252
Yeah? Why not?

00:42:25.266 --> 00:42:27.212
'Cause your misery is the whole point.

00:42:27.318 --> 00:42:29.222
It's too much fun to watch.

00:42:30.208 --> 00:42:32.702
Knowing how your daddy died for you,

00:42:32.710 --> 00:42:34.503
How he sold his soul.

00:42:34.628 --> 00:42:35.743
I mean,

00:42:35.748 --> 00:42:37.255
That's got to hurt.

00:42:39.868 --> 00:42:41.792
He's all you ever think about.

00:42:41.797 --> 00:42:43.822
You wake up, and your first thought is

00:42:43.827 --> 00:42:45.875
"I can't do this anymore".

00:42:46.119 --> 00:42:48.081
You're all lit up with pain.

00:42:48.279 --> 00:42:52.381
I mean, you loved him so
much. And it's all your fault.

00:42:54.539 --> 00:42:56.172
You blew it, Dean.

00:42:56.510 --> 00:42:58.123
I could have given you what you need.

00:42:58.127 --> 00:42:59.532
What do I need?

00:43:00.998 --> 00:43:02.211
Your father.

00:43:03.868 --> 00:43:05.623
I could have brought him back.

00:43:06.987 --> 00:43:08.313
Your loss.

00:43:08.856 --> 00:43:10.103
See ya, Dean.

00:43:10.106 --> 00:43:12.463
I wish you a nice, long life.

00:43:22.189 --> 00:43:23.173
Hold on.

00:43:45.956 --> 00:43:47.114
Do you still hear it?

00:43:47.759 --> 00:43:48.654
No.

00:43:49.050 --> 00:43:50.091
Is it over?

00:43:56.707 --> 00:43:57.953
It's here!

00:44:04.637 --> 00:44:08.853
You're lucky I've got a soft spot
for lost puppies and long faces.

00:44:10.210 --> 00:44:12.612
I just can't leave you like this.

00:44:12.907 --> 00:44:14.224
Besides,

00:44:14.239 --> 00:44:16.554
You didn't call me here
to bargain for Evan.

00:44:16.716 --> 00:44:17.952
Not really.

00:44:17.967 --> 00:44:19.573
Can you bring him back?

00:44:20.318 --> 00:44:21.543
My dad?

00:44:22.398 --> 00:44:23.893
Of course I can,

00:44:23.907 --> 00:44:25.672
Just as he was.

00:44:26.538 --> 00:44:28.963
Your dad would live
a long, natural life,

00:44:29.109 --> 00:44:30.733
Like he was meant to.

00:44:31.297 --> 00:44:33.532
That's a promise. What about me?

00:44:33.538 --> 00:44:35.472
I could give you 10 years,

00:44:35.480 --> 00:44:38.344
10 long, good years with him.

00:44:38.548 --> 00:44:40.164
That's a lifetime.

00:44:40.389 --> 00:44:42.213
The family could be together again.

00:44:42.229 --> 00:44:44.542
John, Dean, Sammy...

00:44:44.936 --> 00:44:47.851
The Winchester boys all reunited.

00:44:52.420 --> 00:44:53.192
Look,

00:44:53.480 --> 00:44:55.521
Your dad is supposed to be alive.

00:44:56.487 --> 00:44:58.112
You're supposed to be dead.

00:44:58.920 --> 00:45:00.994
So, we'll just set things straight,

00:45:01.448 --> 00:45:03.782
Put things back in their natural order,

00:45:04.108 --> 00:45:06.595
And you get 10 extra years on top.

00:45:07.088 --> 00:45:08.824
That's a bonus.

00:45:17.686 --> 00:45:18.801
You think you could...

00:45:25.358 --> 00:45:26.952
Throw in a set of steak knives?

00:45:28.998 --> 00:45:32.262
You know, this smartass
self-Sefense mechanism of yours...

00:45:39.417 --> 00:45:40.771
Dean...

00:45:40.778 --> 00:45:42.282
Now you're really trapped.

00:45:43.297 --> 00:45:44.172
That's got to hurt.

00:45:44.179 --> 00:45:46.762
Let me out now.

00:45:46.766 --> 00:45:47.523
Sure.

00:45:47.528 --> 00:45:50.091
We just got to make a
little deal here first.

00:45:50.096 --> 00:45:51.875
You call off your hellhound

00:45:52.009 --> 00:45:53.313
And let Evan go.

00:45:54.139 --> 00:45:55.364
Then I'll let you go.

00:45:55.956 --> 00:45:58.525
I can't break a binding contract.

00:45:59.547 --> 00:46:01.451
And by "can't," you
mean "don't want to"?

00:46:02.666 --> 00:46:03.944
Last chance.

00:46:04.788 --> 00:46:07.391
Evan and his wife get to
live to a ripe old age.

00:46:07.967 --> 00:46:09.072
Going...

00:46:09.547 --> 00:46:11.282
Going... Let's talk about this.

00:46:11.288 --> 00:46:12.202
Okay, gone.

00:46:15.536 --> 00:46:16.722
Stay inside the circle!

00:46:26.587 --> 00:46:28.141
Come on, Dean...

00:46:30.048 --> 00:46:31.065
What are you doing?

00:46:31.150 --> 00:46:32.793
Oh, you're just gonna
go on a little trip.

00:46:35.090 --> 00:46:36.241
Way down south.

00:46:36.248 --> 00:46:38.212
Look, forget Evan. Think of your dad.

00:46:42.248 --> 00:46:43.503
Regna terrae,

00:46:43.746 --> 00:46:46.121
Cantate deo, psallite domino.

00:46:46.578 --> 00:46:48.875
Qui fertur super caelum caeli

00:46:48.889 --> 00:46:50.452
Ad orientem,

00:46:50.460 --> 00:46:53.891
Ecce dabit vocem suam, vocem virtutis.

00:46:53.900 --> 00:46:56.255
Tribuite virtutem deo.

00:46:56.259 --> 00:46:59.275
Qui fertur super caelum
caeli ad orientem,

00:47:04.319 --> 00:47:05.951
Circle's broken! Come on!

00:47:12.038 --> 00:47:13.282
Omnis fallaciae,

00:47:13.599 --> 00:47:15.503
Libera nos domine.

00:47:20.817 --> 00:47:22.994
Hostis humanae salutis.

00:47:25.898 --> 00:47:27.313
Wait!

00:47:51.889 --> 00:47:53.271
What the hell was that for?

00:47:53.398 --> 00:47:54.802
Sealing the deal.

00:47:54.807 --> 00:47:56.083
I usually like to be warned

00:47:56.088 --> 00:47:58.072
Before I'm violated with demon tongue.

00:47:58.148 --> 00:47:59.855
Evan Hudson is free.

00:48:00.128 --> 00:48:03.302
He and his wife will live long
lives. How do I know you're not lying?

00:48:03.307 --> 00:48:05.362
My word is my bond. Oh, really?

00:48:05.366 --> 00:48:07.132
It is when I make a deal.

00:48:07.416 --> 00:48:08.884
It's the rules.

00:48:09.817 --> 00:48:11.422
You got what you wanted.

00:48:11.826 --> 00:48:13.212
Now let me go.

00:48:24.188 --> 00:48:26.453
You're gonna double-Cross me?

00:48:26.529 --> 00:48:28.893
Funny how I'm the trustworthy one.

00:48:31.038 --> 00:48:32.623
You know,

00:48:32.846 --> 00:48:35.422
You renege, send me to hell,

00:48:35.440 --> 00:48:37.864
Sooner or later I'm gonna climb out, and

00:48:37.867 --> 00:48:40.702
Skinning Evan Hudson will
be the first thing that I do.

00:48:59.139 --> 00:49:00.311
I got to tell you,

00:49:00.737 --> 00:49:03.023
You would have never pulled
that stunt if you knew.

00:49:03.027 --> 00:49:03.822
Knew what?

00:49:04.170 --> 00:49:05.884
Where your dad is.

00:49:06.420 --> 00:49:08.003
You should have made that deal.

00:49:08.708 --> 00:49:10.603
See, people talk about hell,

00:49:10.849 --> 00:49:12.163
But it's just a word.

00:49:12.367 --> 00:49:15.011
Doesn't even come close
to describing the real...

00:49:15.018 --> 00:49:17.702
Shut your mouth, bitch! If
you could see your poor daddy,

00:49:17.710 --> 00:49:19.893
Hear the sounds he makes
'cause he can't even scream.

00:49:19.909 --> 00:49:21.461
How about I send you back there?

00:49:31.779 --> 00:49:32.534
What?

00:49:34.237 --> 00:49:35.804
How did I get here?

00:49:41.188 --> 00:49:44.414
<i>"Key to the Highway" by Big Bill Broonzy</i>

00:49:48.976 --> 00:49:50.644
Demons lie all the time, right?

00:49:50.710 --> 00:49:51.991
Maybe she was lying.

00:49:51.998 --> 00:49:54.045
Come on, is that really what you think?

00:49:56.947 --> 00:49:58.523
How could he do it?

00:49:58.527 --> 00:50:00.741
He did it for you. Exactly.

00:50:00.976 --> 00:50:02.563
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:50:04.400 --> 00:50:05.971
You know, the thought of him,

00:50:07.856 --> 00:50:09.764
Wherever he is right now...

00:50:10.936 --> 00:50:13.335
I mean, he spent his
whole life chasing that

00:50:14.077 --> 00:50:16.034
Yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:50:16.327 --> 00:50:18.284
He should have gone out fighting.

00:50:20.338 --> 00:50:22.414
That was supposed to be his legacy,

00:50:22.416 --> 00:50:23.855
You know?

00:50:25.340 --> 00:50:27.664
Not bargaining with the damn thing.

00:50:29.969 --> 00:50:31.103
Not this.

00:50:31.106 --> 00:50:33.614
How many people do you
think dad saved total?

00:50:33.619 --> 00:50:36.543
That's not the point,
Sam. Evan Hudson is safe

00:50:36.677 --> 00:50:38.644
Because of what dad taught us.

00:50:39.668 --> 00:50:41.302
That's his legacy, Dean.

00:50:42.697 --> 00:50:44.134
Now, we're still here, man,

00:50:44.136 --> 00:50:45.835
So we got to keep going.

00:50:46.666 --> 00:50:47.894
For him.

00:50:54.420 --> 00:50:55.514
Dean? Yeah?

00:50:55.518 --> 00:50:57.414
When you were trapping
that demon, you weren't...

00:50:59.299 --> 00:51:01.144
I mean, it was all a trick, right?

00:51:01.239 --> 00:51:04.271
You never considered actually
making that deal, right?



00:12:04.771 --> 00:12:06.271
